---Create npm access token
---
---Create a new npm access token with customizable permissions, scope restrictions,
---expiration, and CIDR IP range limitations.
---
---To create a stage-only Granular Access Token (GAT), set
---`packages_and_scopes_permission` to `read-write-stage-only` and select
---at least one package or scope. This grants package write access but
---restricts publishing new versions to `POST /-/stage/package/{package-name}`
---(`npm stage publish`). Direct publication is not allowed or automatically staged.
---Requests rejected by the publish-policy check return `403 Forbidden` with
---`E_STAGE_REQUIRED` in the error message. Earlier authentication or package
---authorization checks can return other errors, including `404 Not Found`.
---A maintainer must approve the staged version with 2FA before publication.
---Stage-only is not a valid value for `orgs_permission`.
---
---The publish restriction is separate from `bypass_2fa`. Stage-only tokens
---can be created with either setting, and existing scope, permission, and
---2FA checks still apply to all operations. The restriction does not itself
---remove other package write capabilities, such as changing dist-tags or
---deprecating versions.
---
---**Requirements:**
---- Must be authenticated
---- **Two-factor authentication is required for this endpoint**
---  - If 2FA is enabled on your account, provide the OTP via the `npm-otp` header
---  - If 2FA is not enabled, an email OTP will be sent and must be provided via the `npm-otp` header
---  - For WebAuthn users, the OTP is returned in the `doneUrl` after authentication
---- **Granular Access Tokens with `bypass_2fa: true` are not permitted**
---  to call this endpoint and receive `403 Forbidden`. Token creation
---  (and escalation) requires an interactive 2FA challenge.
---
---**Important notices:**
---- All responses include security notices via the `npm-notice` header regarding token limitations
---
---`POST /-/npm/v1/tokens`
---Errors: BadRequest, Forbidden.
---@param input npm.token.CreateTokenRequest
---@return npm.token.CreateTokenResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:create_token(input) end

---Delete npm access token
---
---Delete an npm access token. The token can be specified as:
---- A UUID (token identifier)
---- An npm-prefixed token (format: `npm_` followed by 36 alphanumeric characters)
---
---**Requirements:**
---- Must be authenticated with a valid Bearer token
---- May require 2FA OTP depending on user settings
---- **Granular Access Tokens with `bypass_2fa: true` are not permitted**
---  to call this endpoint and receive `403 Forbidden`. Token deletion
---  requires an interactive 2FA challenge.
---
---**Web authentication flow:**
---- When `npm-auth-type=web` and `npm-command=token` headers are present and 2FA is required,
---  returns authentication URLs instead of an error
---
---`DELETE /-/npm/v1/tokens/token/{token}`
